{
  "Document": [
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 1,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Window Management"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Tauri gives you granular control over how your application windows look and behave."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Customizing the Window"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "You can configure the window's appearance in "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "tauri.conf.json"
        },
        {
          "Text": " or programmatically in Rust."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Transparency"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Set "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "transparent: true"
        },
        {
          "Text": " to create non-rectangular windows or glass effects."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Frameless"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Set "
        },
        {
          "InlineCode": "decorations: false"
        },
        {
          "Text": " to remove the standard OS title bar and borders, allowing you to build a custom, branded header."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Bold": [
            {
              "Text": "Always on Top"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "Text": ": Keep your app visible above all other windows (useful for toolbars or overlays)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Multi-Window Applications"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Tauri supports creating multiple windows. This is useful for:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "A main dashboard and a separate \"Settings\" window."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Tool palettes that can be dragged to a second monitor."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "UnorderedList": []
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Splash screens that disappear once the app has finished loading."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "CodeBlock": {
        "language": "rust",
        "code": "let window = tauri::WindowBuilder::new(\n    app, \n    \"settings\", \n    tauri::WindowUrl::App(\"settings.html\".into())\n).build()?;"
      }
    },
    {
      "Heading": {
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "Text": "Window Communication"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "Paragraph": [
        {
          "Text": "Windows can communicate with each other by emitting events. One window can tell another window to refresh its data or close itself."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}